description:
Objective: decide, in writing, whether same-user host processes stay outside the protected profile's threat model. Two open points depend on it:
- CQ-R01 follow-up 5: daemon.json's port↔pid binding is not portably verifiable.
- CQ-R08's handoff on CQ-R13, point 3: the per-request daemon.json re-check before a forward has a theoretical TOCTOU window.

Created by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30, when the human moved the non-gating R01 follow-ups out of CQ-R13. This is a spike: its deliverable is a decision, not code.

Deliverable: one decision document under docs/, linked from docs/ARCHITECTURE.md's security notes. It contains:
- the threat-model statement;
- both open points, with references to the code (readDaemonInfo, the guest-session forward path);
- the options considered, each with its reason:
  - a per-platform OS lookup of the port's owner;
  - a daemon-issued nonce over /health;
  - accepting and documenting the gap;
- the decision;
- the follow-up rows to create, if the decision changes behavior.

Out of scope:
- implementing any option;
- .moe edits.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): npm run lint (repo root), and the decision document exists with those sections.

implementationPlan.description:
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: link the record. ARCHITECTURE.md has no security section today, so add `## Security Notes` immediately before `## Error Handling (Current)`. It holds three short bullets:
- the protected profile's threat model: repository content and guest code are in it; same-user host processes and other local users are out of it, so a single-user host is assumed;
- the two accepted gaps, the daemon.json port↔pid binding and the R08 per-request re-check window;
- a relative link to design/protected-profile-threat-model.md.
Change no other line.

Error handling: none at runtime. This is a docs-only change, checked by step 4.
